<div class="doc">
  <section class="doc-hero">
    <div class="doc-hero__crumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span class="doc-sep">/</span><span class="doc-cur">Marble vs. Glass</span></div>
    <div class="doc-hero__head">
      <div class="doc-eyebrow"><span class="doc-eyebrow__ln"></span>Materials Compared<span class="doc-eyebrow__ln"></span></div>
      <h1 class="doc-hero__title">Marble vs. <span class="doc-i">Glass Mosaics</span></h1>
      <p class="doc-hero__sub">Both are premium, hand-cut, and made to order — but they create very different effects. Here's how natural marble and hand-cut glass compare, and how to choose the right one for your space.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="doc-wrap">
    <p class="doc-lead">At iMosaicArt we craft mosaics in <strong>both natural marble and hand-cut glass</strong>, so our advice is genuinely balanced. The right material comes down to the <strong>look you want, where the piece will live, and the feel you're after</strong> — and the two can even be combined in a single design.</p>

    <div class="doc-mats">
      <div class="doc-mat">
        <div class="doc-mat__img"><img src="{{ 'sw-04.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Natural Carrara marble mosaic tesserae" loading="lazy"></div>
        <div class="doc-mat__body">
          <h2 class="doc-mat__t">Natural Marble</h2>
          <p class="doc-mat__d">Cut from genuine marble and stone, each tessera carries natural veining, depth, and earthy warmth. Honed or polished by hand across 40+ tones — from Carrara white to Nero black — marble brings a timeless, architectural, sculptural quality that suits portraits, classical art, floors, and refined interiors.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="doc-mat">
        <div class="doc-mat__img"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0754/6093/5978/files/1_2ddf180e-8e93-44be-bf4d-9ff5e74a8002.png?v=1790505204&width=1200" alt="Hand-cut glass mosaic color range" loading="lazy"></div>
        <div class="doc-mat__body">
          <h2 class="doc-mat__t">Hand-Cut Glass</h2>
          <p class="doc-mat__d">Hand-cut from vitreous glass in a full spectrum of jewel-like tones — including luminous iridescent finishes — glass is non-porous, fully waterproof, and color-stable. It catches and reflects light for vivid brilliance, making it ideal for pools, fountains, backsplashes, and bold, contemporary art.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Side by Side</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">The Comparison</h2>
      <table class="doc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>Natural Marble</th><th>Hand-Cut Glass</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Appearance</td><td>Organic veining, natural depth, matte-to-polished</td><td>Vivid, luminous, light-reflecting</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Color range</td><td>Natural earth tones — whites, greys, beiges, greens, reds, blacks</td><td>Full spectrum, including iridescent finishes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Finish</td><td>Honed or polished stone</td><td>Glossy, matte &amp; iridescent</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Water resistance</td><td>Water-resistant; seal for wet areas</td><td>Non-porous &amp; fully waterproof</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Portraits, classical art, floors, architecture, warm interiors</td><td>Pools, fountains, backsplashes, vibrant modern art, light-filled spaces</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>pH-neutral cleaning; periodic sealing</td><td>Simple wipe; no sealing needed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Feel</td><td>Natural stone — tactile &amp; substantial</td><td>Smooth, bright &amp; jewel-like</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Shared</td><td colspan="2">Both are hand-cut by master artisans, made to order, weatherproof, slip-tested, and covered by a lifetime warranty with free worldwide shipping.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Make the Call</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Which Is Right for You?</h2>
      <div class="doc-choose">
        <div class="doc-choose__card">
          <h3 class="doc-choose__t">Choose Marble if…</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You love natural stone, veining, and earthy tones</li>
            <li>It's a portrait, classical, or fine-art design</li>
            <li>You want a timeless, warm, understated look</li>
            <li>It's for floors, feature walls, or architectural interiors</li>
            <li>You prefer a matte, natural finish over high shine</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-choose__card">
          <h3 class="doc-choose__t">Choose Glass if…</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You want vivid color or iridescent, light-catching finishes</li>
            <li>It's for a pool, fountain, shower, or wet area</li>
            <li>You're after a bold, modern, or abstract statement</li>
            <li>Maximum brightness and reflection matter</li>
            <li>You want a zero-sealing, ultra-low-maintenance surface</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-combine">
        <h2 class="doc-combine__t">Can You Combine Both?</h2>
        <p class="doc-combine__d">Absolutely. Many of our finest commissions blend <strong>marble and glass in a single piece</strong> — the depth and warmth of natural stone paired with the brilliance and color of hand-cut glass. Our designers will help you mix materials so your mosaic has exactly the character you're after.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-sec">
      <div class="doc-sec__eyebrow">Common Questions</div>
      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Marble vs. Glass FAQ</h2>
      <div class="doc-faq">
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Which is more durable, marble or glass mosaic?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Both are extremely durable and fully weatherproof. Glass is non-porous and completely waterproof (ideal for pools); marble is solid natural stone that should be sealed periodically in wet areas. Both are slip-tested and carry a lifetime warranty.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Is marble or glass better for a pool or bathroom?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Glass is usually best for pools, fountains, showers, and bathrooms — it's non-porous, fully waterproof, and stays vivid underwater. Marble also works well in wet areas when sealed, and is often chosen for its natural, timeless look.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Which is better for a portrait or classical mosaic?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Marble is often preferred for portraits and classical art — its natural tones, veining, and depth suit realistic, timeless imagery. Glass is ideal for vivid, luminous, and modern or abstract designs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Is glass or marble mosaic more expensive?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Both are premium, made-to-order materials. Price depends mainly on size, detail, and complexity rather than simply marble versus glass. Share your project with us for an exact quote.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Can marble and glass be combined in one mosaic?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Yes — many iMosaicArt pieces blend both materials, pairing the depth of natural stone with the brilliance of hand-cut glass. Our designers can help you mix them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Does marble need sealing while glass does not?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Correct. Marble is porous, so seal it periodically with a penetrating stone sealer, especially in wet areas. Glass is non-porous and never needs sealing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="doc-cta">
    <div class="doc-cta__inner">
      <h2 class="doc-cta__title">Still Deciding?</h2>
      <p class="doc-cta__text">Tell us about your space and our design experts will recommend the perfect material — or a blend of both — for your custom mosaic.</p>
      <div class="doc-cta__btns">
        <a href="/pages/free-consultation" class="doc-cta__btn">Book a Free Consultation</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="doc-cta__btn doc-cta__btn--ghost">Shop All Mosaics</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
